@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+---
+id: task-002-add-availability-query-to-rental-service
+type: task
+title: "Add availability(query) to rental service"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add `availability(query)` to the rental service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is
+optional. It returns the ids of the equipment of that kind, or of any kind when none is given, that is
+free for the whole period, sorted.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `AvailabilityQuery` (`start`, `end`, optional `kind`) and `availability(query): string[]` to
+  `RentalService` in `src/index.ts`.
+- `availability` validates the period with the same midnight-UTC/whole-day rules as `quote` and `book`
+  (extracted into a shared `validatePeriod` helper), filters equipment by `kind` when given, keeps only
+  items with no booking overlapping the period, and returns their ids sorted (default string sort).
+- Extracted the booking-overlap check used by `book` into a shared `isFree(itemId, startTime, endTime)`
+  helper so `book` and `availability` share one implementation.
+- Test-first: added failing tests for the happy path (filtering by kind, excluding a partially-booked
+  item), no-kind-given, an item whose booking doesn't overlap the query period, and an invalid period,
+  confirmed they failed against the pre-change code, then implemented until all 16 tests in
+  `test/rental-service.test.ts` pass (`node --test`).
+- Documented `availability` in `README.md` alongside the existing `quote`/`book` example and rules
+  paragraph.
+
+## Notes
+
+No new dependencies, booking-id scheme, or validation rule was introduced beyond what dl-001 already
+settled; this change only adds a read path on top of the existing equipment/booking state.
